  "topic": "Template Class Specialization and SFINAE for Conditional Compilation",
  "explanation": "In C++, template specialization allows developers to define custom implementations of a template for specific types or conditions, enabling tailored behavior. Substitution Failure Is Not An Error (SFINAE) is a technique that leverages template specialization and overload resolution to enable or disable template instantiations based on compile-time conditions. Together, these features facilitate writing highly generic, efficient, and type-safe code that adapts to different types or traits without runtime overhead.",
  "syntax": "template <typename T>\nstruct Trait {\n    static constexpr bool value = false;\n};\n\n// Specialization for integral types\ntemplate <typename T>\nstruct Trait<T, typename std::enable_if<std::is_integral<T>::value>::type> {\n    static constexpr bool value = true;\n};\n\n// Function enabled only if T is integral\ntemplate <typename T>\nauto process(T t) -> typename std::enable_if<Trait<T>::value, void>::type {\n    // Implementation for integral types\n}\n\n// Function disabled if T is not integral\ntemplate <typename T>\nauto process(T t) -> typename std::enable_if<!Trait<T>::value, void>::type {\n    // Implementation for non-integral types\n}",
  "code_example": [
    "#include <type_traits>",
    "",
    "// Trait template to detect if a type is integral",
    "template <typename T, typename Enable = void>",
    "struct IsIntegral : std::false_type {};",
    "",
    "// Specialization for integral types using SFINAE",
    "template <typename T>",
    "struct IsIntegral<T, typename std::enable_if<std::is_integral<T>::value>::type> : std::true_type {};",
    "",
    "// Function enabled only for integral types",
    "template <typename T>",
    "auto process(T t) -> typename std::enable_if<IsIntegral<T>::value, void> {",
    "    // Implementation for integral types",
    "    std::cout << t << \" is an integral type.\" << std::endl;",
    "}",
    "",
    "// Function enabled only for non-integral types",
    "template <typename T>",
    "auto process(T t) -> typename std::enable_if<!IsIntegral<T>::value, void> {",
    "    // Implementation for non-integral types",
    "    std::cout << t << \" is not an integral type.\" << std::endl;",
    "}",
    "",
    "int main() {",
    "    process(42);        // Calls integral version",
    "    process(3.14);      // Calls non-integral version",
    "    process(\"hello\"); // Calls non-integral version",
    "    return 0;",
    "}"
  ],
  "example_explanation": "This example demonstrates how template specialization combined with SFINAE enables conditional compilation of functions based on type traits. The IsIntegral template uses std::enable_if to selectively enable function overloads for integral and non-integral types. When 'process' is called with an integer, the integral version is instantiated and executed; for floating-point or string types, the non-integral version is selected. This approach allows writing flexible, type-safe code that adapts to different types at compile time without runtime overhead, exemplifying advanced template programming techniques in modern C++.",
